  <!-- ⚠️ STUB — PREMISES NOT YET VERIFIED. Author the full task with /task-create, which must run its
       own premise check against the code. This project's task files have been wrong 19 times, and the
       2026-09-18 accuracy audit found EIGHT open task files carrying a wrong load-bearing sentence
       (notes/task-accuracy-audit-2026-09-18.md). The statements below are copied from the register
       entry and the finding that produced it; treat every file path, line number and behavioural claim
       as UNCHECKED until /task-create has verified it. -->

  <prompt>`ExternalParticipationService.QueryActiveOrgIdsAsync`'s private overload catches query faults and non-success statuses and returns an EMPTY LIST; only the public overload's token/API-url acquisition can throw. So an HTTP 500/403 or a timeout on the `sprk_contactorganization` query reaches `AccessibleRecordSetService.ReadActiveOrgMembershipsAsync` as a successful read of zero organisations (`Unreadable: false`), which the FR-23 deny veto cannot distinguish from "this subject belongs to no organisation". Every deny row keyed on an organisation the subject belongs to stops matching. Contact-keyed rows still apply, so the ethical wall narrows rather than vanishes — but silently, and this is exactly the case the veto's own documentation claims to cover.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer, C#/.NET, the external access evaluator.</role>
  <goal>A junction-query fault is distinguishable from "no organisations" on the veto path, and the deny veto fails CLOSED when the organisation axis cannot be evaluated — without changing the additive org-grant term, which deliberately wants empty-on-fault so a read failure cannot GRANT access.</goal>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="register ISS-019">The additive callers MUST keep empty-on-fault. Two consumers, inverted fail directions; one shape cannot serve both.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Fail closed on every term that cannot be evaluated.</constraint>
    <constraint source="task 043">The hole PRE-DATES 043. What 043 briefly did was worse than leaving it alone: it documented and unit-tested the property as HELD, using a double that throws where the real path does not. Do not repeat that — the test double must model the real empty-on-fault behaviour.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <notes>Suggested fix on file: a `QueryActiveOrgIdsOutcomeAsync` (ids + `Unreadable`) consumed by the veto path only. Register: `notes/defer-issues.md` § ISS-019. Related: tasks 042, 043.</notes>
</task>
